<h1>Jetson WireGuard kernel modules</h1>
<p>The NVIDIA tegra kernels ship with <code>CONFIG_WIREGUARD</code> compiled
out, so netbird runs userspace wireguard-go on Jetson. These per-kernel
module sets switch it to kernelspace — roughly 2× the throughput at lower
CPU. Built from pinned kernel.org sources, checksummed, exact vermagic.
Release {{ goat_get_kmod_release_tag }}.</p>

<h2>Install (on the Jetson)</h2>
<pre>curl -fLO https://{{ goat_get_hostname }}/{{ goat_get_kmod_www_subdir }}/jetson-wireguard-kmod-$(uname -r).tar.gz
tar xzf jetson-wireguard-kmod-$(uname -r).tar.gz
cd jetson-wireguard-kmod-$(uname -r)
sudo ./install.sh
sudo systemctl restart netbird
netbird status | grep "Interface type"    # expect: Kernel</pre>
<p>No artifact for your <code>uname -r</code>? The tarball's README covers
building for other kernels (~10 min on-device). Uninstall/rollback:
<code>sudo ./install.sh uninstall</code> then follow its printed steps.</p>

<h2>Artifacts</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>File</th><th>Kernel / platform</th></tr>
{% for asset in goat_get_kmod_assets %}
<tr><td><a href="{{ asset }}">{{ asset }}</a></td>
<td>{% if '5.15.148' in asset %}Jetson AGX Orin (JetPack 6.x){% elif '6.8.12' in asset %}Jetson AGX Thor (JetPack 7.x){% else %}checksums{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p>Verify: <code>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing</code>.
Modules are GPL-2.0; each tarball carries LICENSE + PROVENANCE.md with the
pinned upstream source hashes.</p>
